From 7fb8b332b28979650861f49fbe2a98ebc4c2abb9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: MSEF audit fixes <audit@example.invalid>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 12:48:37 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] MSEFv2 harness fixes from evidence audit

- KRE: port 8080 (gunicorn), /remediate route, audit log on PVC, fixed RBAC
  binding, namespace allowlist, MSEF-rule gate, revocation by removing bindings
  (never granting), per-pod quarantine label, confirmed-state MTTC, sync/async
  modes for C4/C5, every alert audited; image tag v2.1.0 + build/sign workflow
- Falco: 10 namespace-scoped rules in deployed customRules; undeployed .txt removed
- Runtime tests: 10 scenarios regenerated (fixed filenames, dedicated attack SA,
  emptyDir for write tests, TEST-NET targets, attack-start markers), scenarios.tsv
- Runtime harness: unified detection+containment measurement, Wilson/t CIs,
  OFPR from benign windows, no harness-side deletion before verification
- Fuzzer: seeded, distinct, composed operators, quantity and transitive-RBAC
  operators, expected decisions, positive control
- Admission oracle (MBR/SPR): explicit denial parsing, ERROR excluded, control required
- Overhead: in-process client, warm-up, failures recorded, apiserver histograms,
  resource sampling; analyze_latency.py for Welch/MW/d/bootstrap from raw samples
- Ablation: verifies cluster state and runs real harnesses; literals removed
- PES/DES fail on missing inputs; DOCX generators with literals replaced by
  export_results_tables.py; v1 results archived
